\textbf{Key results:}
\begin{enumerate}
  \item \textbf{Scalar Aggregate LP} ($r=1$): forces proportional IRFs
        across shocks (constant ratio $\omega_k/\omega_{k'}$), leading to
        severely biased estimates when shocks have different persistence
        (Section~9).

  \item \textbf{OLS Algebraic Identity} (Proposition~\ref{prop:ols_identity}):
        for any invertible $\Omega$, Direct OLS $\equiv$ Aggregate OLS in
        \emph{every} sample---even with a misspecified $\Omega$ (Section~10).

  \item \textbf{Ridge Divergence} (Proposition~\ref{prop:ridge}):
        Ridge ($\lambda > 0$) breaks the identity whenever $\Omega\Omega'
        \neq I$.  Direct Ridge has lower RMSE than Aggregate Ridge,
        confirming that the structural parameterisation aligns better with
        the DGP (Section~11--12).
\end{enumerate}

